t they might have originally  been planned as an easter egg too  Disney's animated movie gigantic an  adaptation of Jack and the Beanstalk  which was few to release the same year  as onward until it was cancelled Tom  Holland and Chris Pratt are the voices  of Ian and barley in onward but as  actors they're both particularly well  known for their portrayals of spider-man  and star-lord in the Marvel Cinematic  Universe and so it's inevitable that  Pixar has squeezed numerous Marvel  references and easter eggs into the  movie first of all on Barley's jacket  there's an Infinity Gauntlet  much like the one famously wielded by  Thanos in Marvel's infinity saga there's  also a sticker with the same design plus  the word gauntlet underneath it on the  back of the passenger seat inside  Barney's van the tiny red skull pin on  Bally's jacket could be a nod to the  Marvel villain  skull who becomes the guardian of the  soul stone in the Marvel verse before  this red skull was the head of Hydra in  the MCU and there's a potential nod to  that organization by the Hydra badge on  Barney's jacket right trap though of  course Hydra is also a deadly multi  headed serpent from Greek and Roman  mythology as well as a Dungeons &amp;  Dragons monster more on D&amp;D Easter eggs  later and the Phoenix gem which brings  the brothers father back to life is  orange colored just like the MCU soul  stone in onward the gem gives in and  barley our data interact with their dead  father and an Avengers infinity war the  soul stone temporarily allowed Thanos to  communicate with his dead daughter  Gamora when he was in the soul world and  Varley who's voiced by Chris Pratt  shares a similar characteristic with  Pratt's MCU character star-lord aka  Peter quill both characters have a love  of mixtapes and both of them had a  traumatic experience as a child when one  of their parents died in onward barly  regrets that he didn't go in to say  goodbye to his father when he was ill  because he was scared of all the tubes  and how unwell he was and when his  mother was about to die in guardians of  the galaxy as a child Peter quill  couldn't bear to hold her hand or look  at her something he would also later  regret Ian who's voiced by Tom Holland  was red and blue colors just like  spider-man who he plays in the MCU and  when Ian says he'll do whatever it takes  to meet his dad it echoes a famous line  for avengers endgame this is the fight  of our lives whatever it takes  onward also includes many hats hips to  other fantasy pop culture and movies  when Ian visits a fast-food restaurant  there's a sign for second breakfast a  nod to JRR Tolkien's The Hobbit in which  Bilbo Baggins likes to eat a second  breakfast something also true the  hobbits and Peter Jackson's Lord of the  Rings trilogy what about breakfast  you've already had it we've had one yes  what about second breakfast and the lor  on varley's quest mixtape is possibly  another nod to Lord of the Rings Farley  later plays a special mixtape titled  rise to Valhalla when he sends his  beloved Van Guinevere off on her final  mission Valhalla is a sacred place in  Norse mythology where many fallen  warriors go to after death the details  in this scene are perfect with Barley's  parking tickets fluttering  the windows giving the sense that  Guinevere has wings and the sound of the  Vans tires on the stones creates a  galloping sound as if she is riding into  battle Dungeons and Dragons is also a  huge inspiration for onward there's  Barley's quest of your role-playing game  complete with a guide that resembles a  D&amp;D manual with spell casting  instructions and the cover of the book  cleverly foreshadows an important moment  later in the movie on Barley's jacket  there's a d20 dice which for anyone  unfamiliar is a 20-sided dice used in  Dungeons and Dragons Bolly also has a  d20 die stitching with lightning bolts  on his jacket sleeve the gelatinous cube  which Ian and barley encounter after  they venture into some caves is a  classic D&amp;D monster taken directly from  the game the oozing cube is an  antagonist that can absorb and digest  the victims it traps and the many other  murderous traps in the caves corridors  give this scene an Indiana Jones vibe  together with the way that Inn and  barley pulled their fathers legs through  the closing stone door just in the nick  of time  much like Indies famous hat grab in the  Temple of Doom another eighties  reference comes at the end of onward  when instead of driving off in volleys  van along the road the van flies away  with the power of magic mimicking the  end of Back to the Future when Doc  returns with his time machine car from  the future and then he Marty and  Jennifer fly away instead of driving  down the road and that back to the  future reference seems especially  fitting given the recent deep fake of  Tom Holland as Marty McFly as always in  every Pixar film there's a cameo from  John Ratzenberger who's one of the  construction workers that yells at  barley when he's getting in the way of  the demolition of the stone fountain  towards the end of the movie office of  Broncos called him for duty with the  police reporting that there's an a.1 1/3  in progress a 1 1 3 is a regular Pixar  Easter Egg that's a tribute to the  California Institute of the Arts  classroom where many of Pixar's animator  studied in Ian and Bali's kitchen  there's a nod to Disney's Sleeping  Beauty and Maleficent with an Aurora  branded washing up liquid and on one of  the shelves in Ian's room there's a  wooden dinosaur figure that resembles  the mysterious Pecola  different Pixar's the good dinosaur  onward is also chock-full of sign and  brand gags great pans and other  pop-culture references in the opening  sequence as a scene in an arcade where a  Center is playing a game called prance  prance revolution a play on the music  video game dance dance revelution at  home the boy's mother Laura uses way  strong chocolate flavor protein powder  for our smoothies and Ian eats trolley  Oh cereal are likely pan on Cheerios  other brand-name gags include cloak and  cola clearly coca-cola mountain doom  onwards version of Mountain Dew which is  also a nod to Lord of the Rings Mount  Doom and saturated a pan on Gatorade  it's also funny that the troll at a toll  booth works for the under bridge  transportation authority a joke about  how trolls in some fairy tales like  three Billy Goats Gruff wait underneath  bridges to prey on those who try to  cross and it also made me chuckle when I  noticed you can either pay the troll  with cash or a riddle now what other  Easter eggs or cool details do you spot  in onward and do you have any theories  on where the movie fits into the Pixar  universe leave your thoughts in the  comments below  if you enjoyed this don't forget to  leave a like and subscribe for all my  new videos tap left for another Pixar  video or tap write for something you're  sure to like thanks for watching and see  you next time you PK movie lovers
 

